{"title":"New 21 Game","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"Alice plays the following game, loosely based on the card game \"21\".\nAlice starts with 0 points and draws numbers while she has less than k points. During each draw, she gains an integer number of points randomly from the range [1, maxPts], where maxPts is an integer. Each draw is independent and the outcomes have equal probabilities.\nAlice stops drawing numbers when she gets k or more points.\nReturn the probability that Alice has n or fewer points.\nAnswers within 10-5 of the actual answer are considered accepted.\n \n## Examples\n\n### Example 1:\n\n```text\nInput: n = 10, k = 1, maxPts = 10\nOutput: 1.00000\n```\nExplanation: Alice gets a single card, then stops.\n\n### Example 2:\n\n```text\nInput: n = 6, k = 1, maxPts = 10\nOutput: 0.60000\n```\nExplanation: Alice gets a single card, then stops.\nIn 6 out of 10 possibilities, she is at or below 6 points.\n\n### Example 3:\n\n```text\nInput: n = 21, k = 17, maxPts = 10\nOutput: 0.73278\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 0 <= k <= n <= 10^4\n- 1 <= maxPts <= 10^4\n","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def new21Game(self, n: int, k: int, maxPts: int) -> float:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().new21Game","parameters":[{"name":"n","type":"int"},{"name":"k","type":"int"},{"name":"maxPts","type":"int"}],"returnType":"float","tests":[{"input":[10000,8614,7400],"expected":0.32115952679227167},{"input":[108,60,626],"expected":0.08600446456298874},{"input":[1087,815,6363],"expected":0.04875895427392066},{"input":[1117,580,1155],"expected":0.768807051915113},{"input":[1198,472,8553],"expected":0.089811188132375},{"input":[121,63,4749],"expected":0.012586909937346551},{"input":[1224,265,4441],"expected":0.22940593747555602},{"input":[1228,731,656],"expected":0.941660327757565},{"input":[1250,1020,8990],"expected":0.028779022116794534},{"input":[1253,165,8632],"expected":0.12857814705496162},{"input":[1278,1000,374],"expected":0.9347436418251434},{"input":[1341